nodecode-redaction-pack is a rewrite of pierrenode's pierrenode/hermes-redaction-pack:

https://github.com/pierrenode/hermes-redaction-pack
commit febd8bfe9971a3242d0ca18e8e7ca71d685d503b
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 pierrenode (LICENSE)

The plugin handed 71 vendor-prefixed regexes to Hermes's secret redactor through
one additive seam, register_redaction_patterns, and registered nothing else. This
rewrite keeps the table row for row -- vendor, token name, the same pattern, and
the source it came from -- and drops the Python: the patterns are compiled by
cl-ppcre and applied at the seam Nodecode does have, the advice on the fold that
projects the event log onto the provider-shaped messages of one turn. The user
text of every message and every tool result is masked on a copy on its way out;
the log keeps the originals. The two mask shapes are the original's -- the first
six and last four characters in ordinary text, a non-reusable sentinel for a
tool result -- and a matcher that throws passes the text through, as the
original's fail-open posture did. What was left out: the plugin's own seam, which
Nodecode does not have, so a mask reaches the provider and not literally every
line of the log this image writes; the formats the original left out on purpose
stay out for the same reasons, and the newest formats whose shape no published
source pins down are not guessed at.
